<div class="tw-p-2 tw-font-alt">
    {{!-- Trained / Basic skills flow into 1–3 width-responsive columns (#267).
         auto-fit makes the grid track count follow the PANEL width (not the
         viewport): it collapses to a single column on a narrow sheet and caps
         at three via the max(min-col, container/3) idiom (gap = 0.5rem ⇒ two
         gaps subtracted at the 3-column breakpoint).

         Floor is 22rem, DERIVED rather than tuned (#267). Every skill row is one
         thin strip (it no longer wraps to a second line), so the floor is that
         strip's fixed chrome plus the longest name: ~226px of chrome on the 4-pip
         lines (DH2e/BC/OW) — 16px row padding + 2px border + 12px grid gaps + 40px
         score track + 92px indicator strip (4 × 20px pips + gaps/padding/border) +
         16px icon + 10px inner gaps + ~44px for the dice and favourite buttons —
         plus ~126px for the longest name and its suffix ("Sleight of Hand (Ag)" at
         0.85rem). 22rem (352px) holds both, so auto-fit drops 3 → 2 → 1 before any
         name would have to end in an ellipsis. The earlier 14rem / 10rem / 20rem
         floors sat below a whole strip, which is why names clipped or rows wrapped.
         `min(22rem, 100%)` keeps a single column inside a panel narrower than one
         strip (it would otherwise overflow); there the name, in a minmax(0, 1fr)
         track, ends in an ellipsis. Pairs with tw-shrink-0 on the row's trailing buttons.
         Skills render from the flat `standard` list in row-major order rather
         than the old fixed two-array column split. --}}
    <div class="tw-grid tw-gap-2 tw-relative" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(max(min(22rem, 100%), calc((100% - 1rem) / 3)), 1fr));" data-testid="skills-responsive-grid">
        {{#each skillLists.standard as |entry|}}
            {{> systems/wh40k-rpg/templates/actor/partial/skill-row.hbs entry=entry}}
        {{/each}}
    </div>

    {{!-- DH2e has no separate "Advanced Skills" tier; advancedUntrained is now empty and
         every standard skill renders in the responsive grid above. See issue #2. --}}
</div>
